  "result": "If I could change the world in one way, I would guarantee truly universal access to high-quality education\u2014right from early childhood through adulthood\u2014tailored to each learner\u2019s needs and aspirations.  \n\nWhy this one change?  \n\u2022 Multiplier effect: Educated individuals are more likely to secure stable employment, make healthier choices, and invest in their children\u2019s futures.  \n\u2022 Poverty reduction: Literacy and vocational skills break cycles of intergenerational poverty, boosting local economies and narrowing inequality.  \n\u2022 Health and well-being: Educated communities enjoy lower rates of infectious disease, better maternal and child health, and greater life expectancy.  \n\u2022 Social cohesion: Critical thinking and exposure to diverse perspectives foster tolerance, reduce prejudice and conflict, and strengthen democratic participation.  \n\u2022 Innovation and sustainability: A broadly educated populace accelerates technological breakthroughs, effective governance and collective solutions to climate change, resource management and public-health crises.  \n\nBy ensuring that every person\u2014regardless of geography, gender, economic background or ability\u2014can learn, grow and apply their talents, we set off a positive domino effect across virtually every challenge we face: from environmental stewardship and social justice to economic resilience and global peace.",
